MultiFile Approach:
1. gcc main.c sum.c diff.c pdt.c div.c -c   -> creates object file
   gcc *.c -c

2. gcc main.o sum.o diff.o pdt.o div.o -o all.exe   -> linkes to create executable file
   gcc *.o -o all.exe

3. ./all.exe   -> to run and output is printed

makefile concepts:

1. target : dependencies
   <tab>commands to generate target

2. make clean  -> to clean all the object and exe files

3. make  -> only first target is compiled

4. make run  -> compiles and runs all the targets at a time

SPECIAL VARIABLES:

1. gcc $^ -c  -> considers all the files in the dependency
2. gcc $< -c  -> considers 1st file in the dependency
3. gcc $@     -> executable file is generated

USER CREATED VARIABLES:

Eg:
1. SRCS = main.c sum.c diff.c pdt.c div.c
object.o : $(SRCS)
   gcc $^ -c
all.exe : $(OBJS)
   gcc $^ -o $@
run: all.exe
   ./all.exe